      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re-reading through the test code, I don\u0027t think the test actually checks what the original value of the mode is, so it doesn\u0027t really check if it is overriden or preserved per say, only that the final mode is correct.\n\nQuickly changing the modes in the original code tests, it still passes, so I am confident that it was overwritting.\n\nIn theory the original test should have checked what the original mode was (0666) to confirm overwritting was occuring.\n\nThe new code updates the related test expectations, and which infers preservation, since the value is as expected (0666) instead of what is supposed to be written (0777).\n\nIf we wanted to be pedantic we could add a non-tabled test that explicitly pulls out the existing mode from the file, fiddles some bits, tries to write it and see if the mode changes, but that feels excessive, since we can infer preservation since we know what the original mode should be and it is different than what is being written.\n\nBriefly looking at docs it looks like os.WriteFile doesn\u0027t change the perm mode if the file already exists, so this was a bug in my original implementation and MatchesReal is missing coverage, which is why it isn\u0027t causing a test behaviour change... Giving my past self the benefit of the doubt here I assume I forgot to add it, since the overwrite test case is the last in the table.",
